---
description: Lodestone contributor conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) at the repository root. Summarized rules:

- Conventional Commits; small, focused commits; feature-named branches.
- Modules in `src/`, `tests/` and `scripts/` stay <= 500 lines with SPDX Apache-2.0 headers.
- Never edit existing files in `src/lodestone/storage/migrations/`; add a new numbered SQL file.
- Storage (`lodestone.storage`) stays below retrieval (`lodestone.lanes` and later fusion). Honor `importlinter.ini` layer contracts; do not import `lodestone.cli` from below.
- Tests named with FR IDs (`test_fr_001_...`). Default tests: no network, no paid APIs.
- Never weaken, skip or delete a CI check. Coverage gate is 80% (`--cov-fail-under=80`).
- OpenSpec: propose → apply → `openspec validate --strict` → archive only after merge on `main`. Change names are verb-noun feature slugs.
- Evidence in `docs/evidence/<feature>.md`; `docs/PROGRESS.md` rows by feature.
- Cursor OpenSpec skills are under `.cursor/skills/`; commands are `/opsx-propose`, `/opsx-apply`, `/opsx-archive`, `/opsx-explore`, `/opsx-sync`, `/opsx-update`.
